DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260424T180000
LOCATION:Evans Auditorium
GEO:45.452273;-122.669241
SUMMARY:Music Colloquium: Dr. Kerry McCarthy
DESCRIPTION:Tudor Singers on the Road  We hear a lot about Renaissance co
 mposers\, but Dr. Kerry McCarthy will talk about the people who actually 
 sang their music and brought it to life\, sometimes in quite challenging 
 circumstances\, and how touring as a musician with Henry VIII wasn't all 
 that different from touring with Taylor Swift!Kerry McCarthy is a musicia
 n and author who has published widely on the English Renaissance\, includ
 ing award-winning new biographies of the composers William Byrd and Thoma
 s Tallis. She is now writing her fourth book\, an exploration of the live
 s of professional singers in Tudor England. She lives in Portland\, where
  she was born and raised.This performance will be live streamed here. (ht
 tps://vimeo.com/event/4079258)  &#160\;Parking at Lewis &amp\; Clark - Fo
 r events in Evans Auditorium\, Agnes Flanagan Chapel\, or Diane Gregg Pav
 ilion\, enter at Gate 2 and park in Upper Griswold\, Lower Griswold\, or 
 Fir Acres Lots (see: campus map (https://www.lclark.edu/live/files/7676-c
 ampus-map)).Parking permits are required during the academic year between
  Monday through Friday\, 7am to 7pm. Please see the Visiting Campus page 
 (https://www.lclark.edu/visit/parking_and_transportation/visitor_parking/
 ) for additional details. For weekday events before 7pm\, visitors may pu
 rchase day passes online (https://lclark.t2hosted.com/Account/Portal) or 
 via QR codes posted in all major parking lots.  &#160\;This event is part
  of our Premier Event series which features a select number of performanc
 es by LC music faculty and guest artists.
