 class="lw_widget_results lw_widget_results_blurbs"><li class="lw_item_1">
 <div class="lw_blurbs_body"><p class="p1" style="font-size: 15px\; line-h
 eight: 1.5\;"><strong>We are committed to making our events accessible to
  all needs and abilities.</strong> If you have a disability that may impa
 ct your academic performance\, you may request accommodations by meeting 
 with the Office of Student Accessibility staff and submitting documentati
 on on the <a href="https://www.lclark.edu/offices/student-accessibility/" target="_blank" rel="
 noopener">Office of Student Accessibility website</a>. Please be aware th
 at the process for evaluation and implementation of accommodations could 
 take 2-3 weeks\, so please be in touch with the OSA as soon as possible. 
 Email <a href="mailto:access@lclark.edu">access@lclark.edu</a> with any a
 dditional questions or concerns.</p></div></li></ul></div><hr /><h2><stro
 ng>About the Instructors</strong></h2><p style="line-height: 1.5\;"><stro
 ng><picture class="lw_image lw_image92745 lw_align_right"><source type="i
 mage/webp" srcset="https://www.lclark.edu/live/image/scale/2x/gid/91/widt
 h/225/height/225/crop/1/src_region/115\,96\,895\,876/92745_Elizabeth-Hoke
 .webp 2x\, https://www.lclark.edu/live/image/scale/3x/gid/91/width/225/he
 ight/225/crop/1/src_region/115\,96\,895\,876/92745_Elizabeth-Hoke.webp 3x
 " data-origin="responsive"/><source type="image/jpeg" srcset="https://www
 .lclark.edu/live/image/scale/2x/gid/91/width/225/height/225/crop/1/src_re
 gion/115\,96\,895\,876/92745_Elizabeth-Hoke.rev.1645484307.jpg 2x\, https
 ://www.lclark.edu/live/image/scale/3x/gid/91/width/225/height/225/crop/1/
 src_region/115\,96\,895\,876/92745_Elizabeth-Hoke.rev.1645484307.jpg 3x" 
 data-origin="responsive"/><img width="225" height="225" alt="" data-alt="
 " data-decoration="true" src="https://www.lclark.edu/live/image/gid/91/wi
 dth/225/height/225/crop/1/src_region/115\,96\,895\,876/92745_Elizabeth-Ho
 ke.rev.1645484307.jpg" srcset="https://www.lclark.edu/live/image/scale/2x
 /gid/91/width/225/height/225/crop/1/src_region/115\,96\,895\,876/92745_El
 izabeth-Hoke.rev.1645484307.jpg 2x\, https://www.lclark.edu/live/image/sc
 ale/3x/gid/91/width/225/height/225/crop/1/src_region/115\,96\,895\,876/92
 745_Elizabeth-Hoke.rev.1645484307.jpg 3x" data-max-w="780" data-max-h="78
 0" loading="lazy" data-optimized="true"/></picture> Elizabeth Hoke\, MFT<
 /strong> is the Clinical Director of Liberation Institute in Portland whe
 re she supervises and provides psychoeducational trainings and workshops.
  She specializes in working with addiction recovery and ADHD\, using a mi
 x of theoretical tools rooted in somatic psychology and biocentric philos
 ophies. Elizabeth co-facilitates ketamine-assisted psychotherapy sessions
  at Rainfall Medicine and co-leads addiction recovery support groups at P
 ortland Psychedelic Society and the Rhizome. She has completed the 100-ho
 ur MDMA Therapy Training program through the Multidisciplinary Associatio
 n for Psychedelic Studies. Elizabeth also co-created the Entheogen Assist
 ed Psychotherapy and Integration Training Series for licensed professiona
 ls at Lewis &amp\; Clark Graduate School Center for Community Engagement 
 in 2021.</p><p style="line-height: 1.5\;"><strong><picture class="lw_imag
 e lw_image95184 lw_align_right"><source type="image/webp" srcset="https:/
 /www.lclark.edu/live/image/scale/2x/gid/91/width/225/height/225/crop/1/sr
 c_region/127\,52\,862\,788/95184_Veronica-Heroic-Journey.webp 2x\, https:
 //www.lclark.edu/live/image/scale/3x/gid/91/width/225/height/225/crop/1/s
 rc_region/127\,52\,862\,788/95184_Veronica-Heroic-Journey.webp 3x" data-o
 rigin="responsive"/><source type="image/png" srcset="https://www.lclark.e
 du/live/image/scale/2x/gid/91/width/225/height/225/crop/1/src_region/127\
 ,52\,862\,788/95184_Veronica-Heroic-Journey.rev.1660079720.png 2x\, https
 ://www.lclark.edu/live/image/scale/3x/gid/91/width/225/height/225/crop/1/
 src_region/127\,52\,862\,788/95184_Veronica-Heroic-Journey.rev.1660079720
 .png 3x" data-origin="responsive"/><img width="225" height="225" alt="" d
 ata-alt="" data-decoration="true" src="https://www.lclark.edu/live/image/
 gid/91/width/225/height/225/crop/1/src_region/127\,52\,862\,788/95184_Ver
 onica-Heroic-Journey.rev.1660079720.png" srcset="https://www.lclark.edu/l
 ive/image/scale/2x/gid/91/width/225/height/225/crop/1/src_region/127\,52\
 ,862\,788/95184_Veronica-Heroic-Journey.rev.1660079720.png 2x\, https://w
 ww.lclark.edu/live/image/scale/3x/gid/91/width/225/height/225/crop/1/src_
 region/127\,52\,862\,788/95184_Veronica-Heroic-Journey.rev.1660079720.png
  3x" data-max-w="735" data-max-h="736" loading="lazy" data-optimized="tru
 e"/></picture> Veronica Vargas\, MA\, LPC</strong> journeys alongside fol
 ks in their path towards healing\, harmony\, and contentment. She finds b
 eauty in witnessing the unfolding of human potential\, and cultivation of
  meaning. Her formal training is in counseling psychology with an emphasi
 s in depth-psychotherapy. Depth-psychotherapy can be defined as a holisti
 c approach that examines all aspects of a person's life\, including dream
 s\, art\, fantasies\, philosophies\, and conscious thoughts. She was heav
 ily influenced by the work of Swiss psychiatrist\, Carl Gustav Jung. In h
 er work as a licensed psychotherapist she assesses the whole person or fa
 mily system by looking at relational and cultural systems\; spirituality\
 ; personal and intergenerational trauma\; systems of oppression\; persona
 l values and how they are or aren't reflected authentically in the person
 's life. She has a private practice in Portland\, Oregon where she offers
  psychotherapy\, dream work\, and psychedelic integration therapy. .</p><
 p style="line-height: 1.5\;">  &#160\;</p><div id="lw_widget_470b39ba" cl
