SUMMARY:Lewis & Clark Orchestra and Choirs
DESCRIPTION:This ten-movement work for choirs\, soloists\, and orchestra 
 offers a powerful and personal meditation on grief and hope. Featured art
 ists: Madeleine Tran\, soprano\; Lisa Neher\, mezzo-soprano\; Brandon Mic
 hael\, tenor\; and Nicolas Vilches '26\, baritone\, with Katherine FitzGi
 bbon\, conductor.  Lewis &amp\; Clark's featured ensembles include Cappel
 la Nova and Community Chorale (Katherine FitzGibbon\, director)\, Voces A
 uream (John Cox\, director)\, and the Lewis &amp\; Clark Orchestra (Lance
  Inouye\, director).Tickets are on sale now! (https://app.arts-people.com
 /index.php?ticketing=lccmd) This performance will be live streamed here. 
 (https://vimeo.com/event/4079258)This concert is dedicated to the memory 
 of Molly Robinson\, beloved Lewis &amp\; Clark faculty member.   &#160\;P
 arking at Lewis &amp\; Clark - For events in Evans Auditorium\, Agnes Fla
 nagan Chapel\, or Diane Gregg Pavilion\, enter at Gate 2 and park in Uppe
 r Griswold\, Lower Griswold\, or Fir Acres Lots (see: campus map (https:/
 /www.lclark.edu/live/files/7676-campus-map)).Parking permits are required
  during the academic year between Monday through Friday\, 7am to 7pm. Ple
 ase see the Visiting Campus page (https://www.lclark.edu/visit/parking_an
 d_transportation/visitor_parking/) for additional details. For weekday ev
 ents before 7pm\, visitors may purchase day passes online (https://lclark
 .t2hosted.com/Account/Portal) or via QR codes posted in all major parking
  lots.
