BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260429T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260429T180000
LOCATION:Corbett House\, Living Room 112
GEO:45.445206;-122.670893
SUMMARY:Documentary Screening: Silent War\, Asian American Reckonings wit
 h Mental Health
DESCRIPTION:The AAPI ERG is hosting a screening of Silent War&#160\;from 
 5:00–7:00 p.m. in Corbett House Living Room 112. While all identities a
 re welcome and encouraged to participate\, the focus of social will focus
  on supporting Asian\, Asian American\, and Pacific Islander identifying 
 communities.Documentary Synopsis:Silent War: Asian American Reckonings wi
 th Mental Health is a groundbreaking documentary that confronts the deep 
 silence surrounding mental illness in Asian American communities. Through
  intimate stories of struggle\, survival\, and healing\, the film explore
 s how cultural stigma\, intergenerational trauma\, racism\, and systemic 
 neglect have shaped the mental health experiences of families from divers
 e Asian backgrounds. Featuring raw personal testimonies\, expert insights
 \, and emotional family reckonings\, Silent War reveals the human cost of
  staying silent—and the power of breaking that silence. At once persona
 l and political\, the film charts a collective journey from shame to resi
 lience\, offering hope for a more inclusive and compassionate mental heal
 th future.  If you have questions\, please direct them to Dr. Amy Wang\, 
 amycwang@lclark.edu (mailto:amycwang@lclark.edu).
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  The AAPI ERG is hosting a screening of 
 <em>Silent War&#160\;</em>from 5:00–7:00 p.m. in Corbett House Living R
 oom 112. While all identities are welcome and encouraged to participate\,
  the focus of social will focus on supporting Asian\, Asian American\, an
 d Pacific Islander identifying communities.</p><p><strong>Documentary Syn
 opsis:</strong></p><p><em>Silent War: Asian American Reckonings with Ment
 al Health</em> is a groundbreaking documentary that confronts the deep si
 lence surrounding mental illness in Asian American communities. Through i
 ntimate stories of struggle\, survival\, and healing\, the film explores 
 how cultural stigma\, intergenerational trauma\, racism\, and systemic ne
 glect have shaped the mental health experiences of families from diverse 
 Asian backgrounds. Featuring raw personal testimonies\, expert insights\,
  and emotional family reckonings\, Silent War reveals the human cost of s
 taying silent—and the power of breaking that silence. At once personal 
 and political\, the film charts a collective journey from shame to resili
 ence\, offering hope for a more inclusive and compassionate mental health
  future.</p><p>  If you have questions\, please direct them to Dr. Amy Wa
 ng\, <a href="mailto:amycwang@lclark.edu">amycwang@lclark.edu</a>.</p>
UID:20260430T000000Z-390776@www.lclark.edu
DTSTAMP:20260417T115957Z
URL:https://www.lclark.edu/live/events/390775-documentary-screening-silen
 t-war-asian-american
LAST-MODIFIED:20260417T190143Z
ATTACH:https://www.lclark.edu/live/image/gid/482/width/80/height/80/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,2592,2596/112812_Silent_War_Poster_2026.rev.1776451091.p
 ng
X-LIVEWHALE-TYPE:events
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:390776
X-LIVEWHALE-TIMEZONE:America/Los_Angeles
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE:https://www.lclark.edu/live/image/gid/482/width/80/heig
 ht/80/crop/1/src_region/0\,0\,2592\,2596/112812_Silent_War_Poster_2026.re
 v.1776451091.png
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE-CAPTION:Silent War
X-LIVEWHALE-SUMMARY:<p>\n  Join the Asian American and Pacific Islander (
 AAPI) ERG for a screening of <em>Silent War\,&#160\;</em>a powerful new d
 ocumentary featuring Asian American voices confronting mental illness and
  the impact of silence. The film explores shame\, resilience\, and hope f
 or a more compassionate mental health future.&#160\;\n</p>
END:VEVENT
