BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260430T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260430T180000
LOCATION:Stamm
SUMMARY:ENVS Spring Poster Celebration
DESCRIPTION:Please join us in celebrating the end of the semester and the
  work that students have conducted in their ENVS and CORE courses this se
 mester! The following classes will be represented in the poster celebrati
 on:ENVS 295 Environmental Engagement: Students will present public commun
 ication materials they created using data collected during community mapp
 ing engagement methods in two Portland city parks - Gabriel Park and Irvi
 ng Park. The materials will both speak to engagement participant's perspe
 ctive and experience with open and public space planning\, and inform the
  public on how to engage with this topic further in Portland.&#160\;  ENV
 S 350 Environmental Theory: Students will present posters summarizing the
 ir environmental praxis projects\, grounding a key theory concept in the 
 real world.  ENVS 400 Senior Seminar: Students will present individual po
 sters on their capstone projects.  ENVS 400 Senior Seminar (North Portlan
 d capstone section): Students will present outcomes of their Albina-based
  senior environmental research\, via individual posters and team-based St
 oryMaps and a new website\, us (http://albinamaps.us/).  ENVS 490 Landsca
 pe Mapping and Monitoring: Students will present their landscape mapping 
 and monitoring results from semester long investigations in land use and 
 land cover changes.  CORE 121 Measuring Environmental Meaning: Students w
 ill present posters summarizing the results of their original team-based 
 environmental surveys.  CORE 121 Take Charge! Tackling Environmental Prob
 lems: Students will present posters summarizing their whole-class proposa
 ls for improving transportation at LC.    This event will be held in Stam
 m\, in Fowler Student Center. Snacks will be provided.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Please join us in celebrating the end o
 f the semester and the work that students have conducted in their ENVS an
 d CORE courses this semester! The following classes will be represented i
 n the poster celebration:</p><ul><li><strong>ENVS 295 Environmental Engag
 ement</strong>: Students will present public communication materials they
  created using data collected during community mapping engagement methods
  in two Portland city parks - Gabriel Park and Irving Park. The materials
  will both speak to engagement participant's perspective and experience w
 ith open and public space planning\, and inform the public on how to enga
 ge with this topic further in Portland.&#160\;  </li><li><strong>ENVS 350
  Environmental Theory</strong>: Students will present posters summarizing
  their environmental praxis projects\, grounding a key theory concept in 
 the real world.  </li><li><strong>ENVS 400 Senior Seminar</strong>: Stude
 nts will present individual posters on their capstone projects.  </li><li
 ><strong>ENVS 400 Senior Seminar (North Portland capstone section)</stron
 g>: Students will present outcomes of their Albina-based senior environme
 ntal research\, via individual posters and team-based StoryMaps and a new
  website\, <a href="http://albinamaps.us/">us</a>.  </li><li><strong>ENVS
  490 Landscape Mapping and Monitoring</strong>: Students will present the
 ir landscape mapping and monitoring results from semester long investigat
 ions in land use and land cover changes.  </li><li><strong>CORE 121 Measu
 ring Environmental Meaning</strong>: Students will present posters summar
 izing the results of their original team-based environmental surveys.  </
 li><li><strong>CORE 121 Take Charge! Tackling Environmental Problems</str
 ong>: Students will present posters summarizing their whole-class proposa
 ls for improving transportation at LC.  </li></ul><p>  This event will be
  held in Stamm\, in Fowler Student Center. Snacks will be provided.</p>
