LOCATION:Zoom
SUMMARY:Belong Cornerstone Webinar: Principles Inform Belonging Work
DESCRIPTION:What does faith have to say about Belonging?  Whether at a hi
 storically religious institution or at a secular school\, religion influe
 nces our approaches to inclusion and difference.  Associations serving re
 ligiously affiliated colleges and universities play a vital role in helpi
 ng institutions remain grounded in mission while managing the changing la
 ndscape of higher education. This webinar will explore observations from 
 associations serving religious institutions and how their campuses are na
 vigating the intersection of faith\, identity\, and belonging.  Featuring
  leaders from associations that represent diverse religious traditions\, 
 the conversation will highlight strategies\, resources\, and approaches t
 hat help institutions stay true to their founding values and foster suppo
 rtive environments for their students. Panelists will share how they see 
 campuses move through complex questions around mission alignment\, studen
 t engagement\, and community building.  Attendees will gain insight into:
 Approaches to supporting student belonging within faith-based frameworks 
  Examples of programs\, initiatives\, and resources offered to member cam
 puses  Opportunities for collaboration and shared learning across institu
 tions    Featuring:Donna Carroll\, Association of Catholic Colleges and U
 niversities  David Hoag\, Council for Christian Colleges &amp\; Universit
 ies  Lamont Anthony Wells\, Network of Evangelical Lutheran Church in Ame
 rican (ELCA) Colleges and Universities  Register Here (https://us06web.zo
 om.us/webinar/register/WN_mFCNRzOsTpCbyUkL3D8Isw?ampDeviceId=bfd0eac0-929
 f-4dd5-8074-8cc2b672cd15&amp\;ampSessionId=1775576497642&amp\;ampDeviceId
 =bfd0eac0-929f-4dd5-8074-8cc2b672cd15&amp\;ampSessionId=1775576497642&amp
 \;_gl=1*1o3bk3z*_gcl_au*MTkzNzkwNjkzNy4xNzcxNTE5OTA0*_ga*MTA5NDY0NjUxMS4x
 NzMyMDQ3MTEw*_ga_L8TBF28DDX*czE3NzU2Njc1MTAkbzExNSRnMSR0MTc3NTY2NzUxNyRqN
 TMkbDAkaDA.#/registration)
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  What does faith have to say about Belon
 ging?</p><p>  Whether at a historically religious institution or at a sec
 ular school\, religion influences our approaches to inclusion and differe
 nce.</p><p>  Associations serving religiously affiliated colleges and uni
 versities play a vital role in helping institutions remain grounded in mi
 ssion while managing the changing landscape of higher education. This web
 inar will explore observations from associations serving religious instit
 utions and how their campuses are navigating the intersection of faith\, 
 identity\, and belonging.</p><p>  Featuring leaders from associations tha
 t represent diverse religious traditions\, the conversation will highligh
 t strategies\, resources\, and approaches that help institutions stay tru
 e to their founding values and foster supportive environments for their s
 tudents. Panelists will share how they see campuses move through complex 
 questions around mission alignment\, student engagement\, and community b
 uilding.</p><p>  Attendees will gain insight into:</p><ol><li>Approaches 
 to supporting student belonging within faith-based frameworks  </li><li>E
 xamples of programs\, initiatives\, and resources offered to member campu
 ses  </li><li>Opportunities for collaboration and shared learning across 
 institutions  </li></ol><p>  Featuring:</p><ul><li>Donna Carroll\, Associ
 ation of Catholic Colleges and Universities  </li><li>David Hoag\, Counci
 l for Christian Colleges &amp\; Universities  </li><li>Lamont Anthony Wel
 ls\, Network of Evangelical Lutheran Church in American (ELCA) Colleges a
 nd Universities  </li></ul><p style="text-align: center\;"><a class="btn-
 small-style-1" href="https://us06web.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_mFCNRzOs
 TpCbyUkL3D8Isw?ampDeviceId=bfd0eac0-929f-4dd5-8074-8cc2b672cd15&amp\;ampS
 essionId=1775576497642&amp\;ampDeviceId=bfd0eac0-929f-4dd5-8074-8cc2b672c
 d15&amp\;ampSessionId=1775576497642&amp\;_gl=1*1o3bk3z*_gcl_au*MTkzNzkwNj
 kzNy4xNzcxNTE5OTA0*_ga*MTA5NDY0NjUxMS4xNzMyMDQ3MTEw*_ga_L8TBF28DDX*czE3Nz
 U2Njc1MTAkbzExNSRnMSR0MTc3NTY2NzUxNyRqNTMkbDAkaDA.#/registration">Registe
 r Here</a></p>
