DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260515T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260515T110000
LOCATION:Amphitheater
SUMMARY:Beatrice M. Cannady Graduation Celebration
DESCRIPTION:Beatrice M. Cannady was the first African-American woman to g
 raduate from Lewis &amp; Clark Law School\, and the first Black woman law g
 raduate in the entire state of Oregon. This event is dedicated to her to 
 honor her remarkable contributions to the legal community and community w
 rit large. Cannady was part of the campaign to repeal Oregon&#8217\;s law
 s denying people of color the right to vote and outlawing Black people fr
 om living in the state\, and she helped write Oregon's first civil rights
  legislation. She was the city's unofficial ambassador between the races\
 , establishing the NAACP's Portland branch. This graduation celebration i
 s to inspire our graduates to follow in this trailblazer's footsteps in c
 reating positive change and advocating for justice. Cannady's legacy remi
 nds us to envision a more just future in the face of adversity and dedica
 te ourselves to bringing it to fruition.  If you are a student graduating
  in 2025\, please RSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/14ysC5vVxeuf
 JCMQD4d8t4y4V3kroHtySSSTRs-fPVN0/edit) by Friday\, April 11\, 2025\, if y
 ou would like to be honored at this event.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<div><i>Beatrice M. Cannady was the first Af
 rican-American woman to graduate from Lewis &amp; Clark Law School\, and th
 e first Black woman law graduate in the entire state of Oregon. This even
 t is dedicated to her to honor her remarkable contributions to the legal 
 community and community writ large. Cannady was part of the campaign to r
 epeal Oregon&#8217\;s laws denying people of color the right to vote and 
 outlawing Black people from living in the state\, and she helped write Or
 egon's first civil rights legislation. She was the city's unofficial amba
 ssador between the races\, establishing the NAACP's Portland branch. This
  graduation celebration is to inspire our graduates to follow in this tra
 ilblazer's footsteps in creating positive change and advocating for justi
 ce. Cannady's legacy reminds us to envision a more just future in the fac
 e of adversity and dedicate ourselves to bringing it to fruition.</i></di
 v><div></div><div></div><div>  If you are a student graduating in 2025\, 
 please <a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/14ysC5vVxeufJCMQD4d8t4y4V
 3kroHtySSSTRs-fPVN0/edit" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-saferedirec
 turl="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://docs.google.com/forms/d/14ysC5
 vVxeufJCMQD4d8t4y4V3kroHtySSSTRs-fPVN0/edit&amp\;source=gmail&amp\;ust=17
 41889535992000&amp\;usg=AOvVaw1Kdu9T130yyyPMlRokxv3J">RSVP here</a> by Fr
 iday\, April 11\, 2025\, if you would like to be honored at this event.</
 div>
