 n" data-max-w="225" data-max-h="225" loading="lazy" data-optimized="true"
 /></picture></p><p style="line-height: 1.5\;">  Kendra Larson grew up in 
 Salem\, OR. She received her MFA in Painting at University of Wisconsin\,
  Madison and has shown her work in venues including the Whatcom Museum (B
 ellingham\, WA)\, the University of Minnesota's Nash Gallery (Minneapolis
 \, MN)\, Boise State University (Boise\, ID)\, and Overture Center for th
 e Arts (Madison\, WI). Her work invites viewers to reimagine their relati
 onship with the natural world\, reignite a sense of wonder\, and advocate
  for environmental care through the language of paint.</p><p style="line-
 height: 1.5\;">  Her work has appeared in publications such as <em>The Be
 ar Deluxe</em> and <em>Tree Sap Magazine</em>. Larson is a past artist in
  residence at Caldera (Sisters\, Oregon)\, New Pacific Studios (Masterton
 \, New Zealand)\, and Fish Factory Creative Centre of Stöðvarfjörður 
 (Iceland). When not in the studio\, she teaches at Clark College and is t
 he Archer Gallery and Clark Art Talks Director. She is represented by Aug
 en Gallery in Portland\, OR and AMcE Creative Arts in Seattle\, WA.&#160\
 ;</p><div id="lw_widget_470b39ba" class="lw_widget lw_widget_type_blurbs 
