LOCATION:Online
SUMMARY:Cultivating Spaciousness and Abundance: Courage to Lead® for Sus
 tainable Growth (Online)
DESCRIPTION:As leaders we are often called to come from a place of perpet
 ual productivity\, bottomless capacity\, always giving and always "on". Y
 et the wholeness of who we are requires periods of reflection\, receiving
  and renewal. When we do not honor this necessary balance\, the wisdom of
  our hearts is harder to hear.What's growing in your life? What needs to 
 be nourished for further growth? What do you want to prune or clear out?H
 ow do we listen to and honor what we need to be whole and in balance amid
  the demands and desires of an abundant life\, in a way that allows for s
 paciousness\, authenticity and joy?How do we tend to the garden of our li
 ves and our work so that we can receive what we need to flourish?  Held d
 uring a time of peak growth and seasonal abundance\, this Courage to Lead
 ® two-day workshop invites us into spacious time for reflection\, connec
 tion\, and inner growth.Together we will…      Pause and cultivate our 
 capacity to be present          Meaningfully engage with ourselves\, othe
 rs and nature with spaciousness and care          Take stock of our relat
 ionship to abundance and consider intentional paths of growth and clearin
 g          Develop skills for holding meaningful conversations and buildi
 ng relational trust          Explore reflective and creative practices in
 cluding the SoulCollage (https://soulcollage.com/about/)® method\, an ex
 pressive arts practice used as a tool for accessing personal and archetyp
 al wisdom      To ensure your SoulCollage (https://soulcollage.com/about/
 )® materials packet arrives before the workshop\, register by June 24.De
 tails &amp\; RegistrationDates and Times: Thursday-Friday\, July 9-10\, 2
 026\, 9:30 a.m.-2:30 p.m. PT\, OnlineFacilitator: Matsya Siosal\, and&#16
 0\;Rafaela Steen\, LCSWRegistration: $225. Includes 9 PDUs or CEUs\, and 
 materials packetRegister Online (https://lclark.tfaforms.net/4735427?epid
 =a1aUY000002Wikj)Scholarship Fund: We strive to keep our Courage retreats
  accessible to all who wish to participate. Please consider making a tax-
 deductible donation (https://engage.lclark.edu/register/gsecgiving?sys:gi
 ft:fund=4dfb9f4e-7351-4d84-91fe-531631c248c7&amp\;sys:gift:notes=Courage%
 20and%20Renewal%20Retreats%20Scholarship%20Fund) to our scholarship fund.
 About the Facilitators Matsya Siosal has developed her skills in leadersh
 ip and facilitation for over 25 years\, including roles with small and la
 rge for-profit corporations\, mission-driven consumer goods companies\, h
 igher education\, and as a consultant and entrepreneur. She has served as
  the director of the Center for Community Engagement at Lewis &amp\; Clar
 k since 2015\, after joining the department in 2010 to work in marketing 
 and program management. Matsya is also co-founder and managing partner of
  Sea-O-Salt Bath Company (http://www.seaosalt.com/). Matsya is an experie
 nced certified facilitator of Courage &amp\; Renewal programs. She has fa
 cilitated Circle of Trust\, Courage to Lead\, and Leading Together worksh
 ops and retreats since 2019\, and is trained as a SoulCollage® (https://
 soulcollage.com/) facilitator. As a facilitator and coach\, Matsya suppor
 ts mission-driven leaders in accessing their authentic voice\, and findin
 g clarity and self-trust so they can show up with wholeheartedness and su
 stainability in their lives and work. Rafaela Steen\, LCSW has been bring
 ing people together for purpose\, support\, and connection for most of he
 r adult life. For the last two decades\, Rafaela has worked as an educati
 onal leader and strengths-based licensed clinical social worker offering 
 consultation\, guidance\, and professional development related to mental 
 health and well-being in K-12 schools and districts. Rafaela is an experi
 enced facilitator\, thought partner\, convener\, and problem solver who s
 ees the importance of meaningful connection and joy within communities. R
 afaela intentionally and strategically creates proactive\, welcoming comm
 unities of care throughout her life\, both personally and professionally.
 New workshops and trainings are added to our calendar regularly. For the 
 latest on professional development related to your specific interests\, s
 ign up for our mailing list! (https://lclark.tfaforms.net/4735441)
