 ualities\, peer education\, and community development. Carson specializes
  in building capacity in sex educators\, creating sexuality education and
  leadership development programming for adolescents\, and developing prog
 rams that center Queer and Trans communities. Carson works at Lewis &amp\
 ; Clark Graduate School as TransActives's Head of Education and Outreach\
 , where he supports transgender\, non-binary\, and other gender expansive
  youth by strengthening the systems that surround them. He received his M
 asters of Education in Human Sexuality from Widener University in 2012 an
 d is currently a PhD student in Education and Leadership at Pacific Unive
 rsity. Carson is a big fan of being on mountains\, in rivers\, and with f
 riends.&#160\;</p><div id="lw_widget_470b39ba" class="lw_widget lw_widget
